  "findings": [
    "Coverage drops by a factor of one trillion as displacement scale falls from 0.01 to 1e-8, but noise remains approximately constant. Tiny interpolation weights are not themselves evidence of amplified noise.",
    "The mean source position remains up to sqrt(2) pixels from the requested point. Correcting its first moment removes affine-scene bias to floating precision.",
    "At scale 1e-5, mean noisy curved-scene RMS across all four CFA layouts and eight seeds falls from about 0.5864 to 0.1277. Noise alone falls about 17 percent.",
    "Balanced +/-0.25-pixel dithers have zero sampling centroids. Their images remain bitwise unchanged despite nonuniform colour coverage, avoiding the flaw in broad density blending.",
    "For curved scenes, the discontinuity falls from about 1.12 to 0.0301 RMS but remains finite. First moments alone cannot account for curvature or changing sampling footprints."
  ],
